The WI-ziruv survey (docs/surveys/axiom-falsifiability.md) recorded four
gaps: no cross-catalogue medium check, no entrypoint-kind test, ADR-0061
ruling 7 unchecked, and WI-kufos's collapsed-row shape unreproduced. Each
now has tests of the same kind as the survey's: a reach check, a checker
control, and a strict xfail naming the item that owns a failure.

| Gap | Test | Holds on | Strict xfail |
|---|---|---|---|
| ADR-0050: one medium, one boundary, across catalogues | core test_medium_families.py: 11 media, 99 members, 13 catalogues | 91 members | c printf/putchar (WI-sofam); js http/net.createServer, Deno.listen (WI-vogos); elixir IO.gets, IO.read, IO.inspect (WI-jofud, new) |
| entrypoint kind names WHAT, evidence_type HOW | one entrypoint by two routes keeps one kind; a callable kind targets a callable | click vs [project.scripts]; flask decorator vs add_url_rule; express named vs inline | a Flask app variable is a main_function entrypoint (WI-dofiz, new) |
| ADR-0061 ruling 7, one persistent taint home | one taint_sinks.d file, two unrelated repos | yes | none |
| WI-kufos: a collapsed row is its group | swap two calls; the caveats and verdict must not move | none | (2) choice caveat on the witness source; (1) INV-dudal withdrawal on the witness sink, the false-clean direction |

The medium map is the judgment ADR-0050 needs, written down once per
family where it can be reviewed. Members are primitives whose documentation
says they cross the medium at the call, always or with default arguments.
Primitives whose medium is set by a required argument or receiver are left
out: unistd.write, fprintf, PrintStream.println. So are the rows INV-dukam
keeps on subprocess for a measured reason: go exec.Command and rust
Command::new. A member may declare an extra arm but may not lack its
medium's boundary. Every member must exist, so a renamed row fails rather
than passing.

Ruling 7's effect on a verdict was already tested by
test_taint_channels_are_read.py (WI-mimap). The survey had not cited it, and
now does.

